message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. 若使用本作，请按下述格式引用。"
type: book
title: "遗忘的边界：有限容量下的记忆、智能与自我 / The Boundary of Forgetting: Memory, Intelligence, and the Self under Finite Capacity"
abstract: >-
  本著作提出“容量级联”框架，用以解释有限容量如何同时塑造记忆、智能与自我。 核心主张：大模型的键值缓存、智能体的上下文窗口与人的记忆并非同构，而是同约束——受同一组信息论限制（压缩、干扰、遗忘），却运行在相差约九个数量级的时间尺度上。遗忘因此不是失败，而是学习得以发生的前提。 结构与证据：25 章、附录 A—K、31 幅图；给出信息瓶颈、率失真、有效容量、表示坍塌与时间尺度分离的形式化；三个载体的失败（位置偏差、上下文漂移、忒修斯现象）被放在同一张表上比较。 诚实的纪律：同约束给出可检验的三条（C1 容量饱和、C2 双时间常数、C3 受限可塑性），任一条测不出即不在主张范围内；双分级与可证伪登记簿随书公开。 边界：同约束不等于同构，跨载体的机制差异不可抹平；“梦=正则化”等主张标为最低等级假说，并写明如何检验。 版本：2026-10-18，201 页，25 章，31 图，附录 A—K；含可复算脚本，内容 CC BY 4.0，代码 MIT。
  Abstract (English). This work presents a “capacity cascade” framework explaining how finite capacity shapes memory, intelligence and the self at once. Core thesis: the KV cache of a model, the context window of an agent and human memory are not isomorphic but iso-constrained — bound by one set of information-theoretic limits (compression, interference, forgetting) across roughly nine orders of magnitude in timescale. Forgetting is therefore the condition of learning, not its failure. Structure and evidence: 25 chapters, appendices A–K, 31 figures; formal treatments of the information bottleneck, rate–distortion, effective capacity, representational collapse and timescale separation; three characteristic failures (position bias, context drift, the Theseus phenomenon) compared in one table. Discipline: iso-constraint is operationalised as three testable conditions — capacity saturation, two time constants, constrained plasticity — and the framework is out of scope if any fails. Boundaries: iso-constraint is not isomorphism; the “dream as regularisation” claim is graded as a hypothesis with a stated test. Edition: 2026-10-18, 201 pages, 25 chapters, 31 figures, appendices A–K.
